 "gossip": {
  "text": "Lamar Jackson is out. The Ravens have ruled him out of Sunday night in Atlanta, so Snoop Huntley starts against a Falcons team that is reportedly feeling confident with Michael Penix Jr. at quarterback. Jesse Minter says he expects Huntley to play well, which is what anyone would say about the backup on Saturday. It gets worse. Cam Jurgens is out with a concussion, Trey Hendrickson has gone from questionable to out with his finger, Ja'Kobi Lane is on injured reserve and Zay Flowers is questionable with a foot. Yesterday this column trusted the gloomy Sunday price over the cheerful February one, and that call looks healthier than Baltimore's roster. Oddly, the line has come in from +3.5 to +3. My guess is the market had already assumed Lamar wouldn't play. Rob and Darren hold four Baltimore tickets between them. I would not want any of them this weekend.\n\nAndy's candle has been snuffed out. Brian Branch is out with an Achilles, and Rock Ya-Sin and Ben Bartch are out too. That leaves a Lions secondary I wouldn't trust against a stiff breeze. Detroit is still giving 5.5 at Arizona, and I think that's too many.\n\nDarren is now on the third chapter of his tragedy. Kyle Dugger is out and Bryan Cook is questionable, so the Bengals are short at safety on top of everything else. Steve, meanwhile, has no new names on Kansas City's injury list for a second day running. He is 4-0 and doing absolutely nothing, which is the most annoying thing a man can do in a pool.",
  "written": "2026-10-10T06:16:17-07:00",
  "based_on": 18
 }
}